# Hellfrost (warlock)
Sci-fi automation hardcore game. C++20 headless engine + React/TypeScript web client, connected via JSON-RPC 2.0 over WebSocket.

## Stack
- **Engine**: C++20, EnTT (ECS), Sol2+Lua5.4, IXWebSocket, cereal, nlohmann/json, magic_enum
- **Web**: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Zustand, Pixi.js, Dockview, Monaco Editor
- **Build**: CMake + `just` task runner. `just run` / `just test-e2e` / `just web-dev`

## Architecture
Web UI → JSON-RPC (:9800) → C++ Handler → EnTT registry → 50ms systems tick → broadcast → Zustand stores → React

Systems order (DO NOT reorder without checking dependencies):
TweeningSystem → PowerSystem → ThermalSystem → EnvironmentSystem → WirelessConnectionSystem → CodeExecutionSystem → ItemsSystem

## Critical Rules
- **Ask questions before implementing**. Never rush to code.
- **Search before creating** — duplicates are the main failure mode.
- **Run `just test-e2e`** after any C++ change. Unit tests are secondary.
- **Never modify** `data/` or `save/` — binary game data.
- **No code comments** unless logic is non-obvious.
- **No docstrings, no error handling for impossible cases, no premature abstractions.**
- Report features as done only after end-to-end verification.

## Key Files
```
include/game/components/frame.hpp     — Frame, Component, Connection, Metadata structs
include/game/attributes.hpp           — Attribute, Modifier, AttributeValue
include/game/component_registry.hpp  — COMPONENT_LIST macro (serialization registry)
include/game/game_manager.hpp        — Systems, registry, spendable pool
src/rpc/handlers/                    — RPC method implementations
scripts/components/                  — Lua component definitions
scripts/blueprints/                  — Lua frame templates
web/src/stores/game.ts               — Primary game state (Zustand)
web/src/rpc/types.ts                 — TypeScript DTOs
```
